        "note": [
          "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of patients who have been treated for mental and behavioural disorders caused by opioids (ICD-10: F11) as the main or secondary diagnosis in accordance with the patient register (inpatient care) that in the same calendar year have collected medicines recommended in the National Board of Health and Welfare's guidelines: buprenorphine (N07BC01), methadone (N07BC02) (excluding substances used for pain relief), or buprenorphine, combinations (N07BC51). The data are presented by year and can be disaggregated by county (based on the county in which the patient was registered during the first hospital admission for the relevant diagnosis), gender and age groups."
